{#
  The top of every page's Markdown: the `.md` a Markdown browser or a
  language model reads. The CMS writes the front matter above this and
  the page's own Markdown below it; a site theme overrides this file to
  change what comes between.

  Autoescaping is off: this is Markdown, not HTML. Print text through
  `escapeMarkdown` so a label stays literal, and a link through `markdownUrl`,
  which gives a page of this site its `.md` URL and leaves any other URL as
  it is.

  `title` is the heading, absent when the page's own Markdown opens with one.
  `bio` is the person the page speaks for, on an author archive and on a solo
  author site's homepage: `name`, `url`, `note` and `links` (each a `label`
  and a `url`). `staticFrontPage` is true on a homepage that is a page. This
  theme prints the bio there only when the homepage lists posts, as its HTML
  does (decision-45); a site theme may print it on a static homepage too.

  A post then says what kind it is, with the data its HTML partials read.
  `event` is an event's `start`, its `end` and its `location`, printed in the
  site's zone as `event.njk` prints them. `cites` are what it answers or cites,
  each a `verb`, a `url` and a `name`, as `reply-context.njk` and
  `citations.njk` name them, with an `author` or `site`, an event's
  `startDate` (in `startZone` when it has one), a `published` date, a
  `location`, and a silo `copy`, each only when it is known. `review` is the
  HTML's review with its words in plain text: `link`, `about`, `by`, `uid`
  and `details`. `location` is where the post was written, only as far as
  Settings > Privacy shares it, in the shape `location.njk` reads. `lang` is
  the post's own language, which its dates are written in.
#}
{% if title %}
# {{ title | escapeMarkdown }}

{% endif %}
{% if event %}
When: {{ event.start | date("datetime", none, lang) }}{{ (" to " + (event.end | date("datetime", none, lang))) if event.end }}

{% if event.location %}
Where: {{ ("Online at [" + (event.location.url | host | escapeMarkdown) + "](" + (event.location.url | markdownUrl) + ")") if event.location.kind == "virtual" else (event.location.name | escapeMarkdown) }}

{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% for cite in cites %}
{{ cite.verb }} [{{ cite.name | escapeMarkdown }}]({{ cite.url | markdownUrl }}){{ (" by " + (cite.author | escapeMarkdown)) if cite.author }}{{ (" · " + (cite.site | escapeMarkdown)) if cite.site }}{{ (", " + (cite.startDate | date("readable", cite.startZone, lang))) if cite.startDate }}{{ (", " + (cite.published | date("readable", none, lang))) if cite.published }}{{ (", " + (cite.location | escapeMarkdown)) if cite.location }}

{% if cite.copy %}
Also in reply to [its copy on {{ cite.copy | host | escapeMarkdown }}]({{ cite.copy }})

{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% if review %}
Review of {{ ("[" + (review.item.name | escapeMarkdown) + "](" + (review.link | markdownUrl) + ")") if review.link else (review.item.name | escapeMarkdown) }}{{ (" (" + (review.about | join(", ") | escapeMarkdown) + ")") if review.about.length }}{{ (", " + (review.by | escapeMarkdown)) if review.by }}{{ (", " + (review.uid | escapeMarkdown)) if review.uid }}

{% if review.details.length %}
{{ review.details | join(" ") | escapeMarkdown }}

{% endif %}
{% if review.rating %}
Rated {{ review.rating }} out of {{ review.best }}

{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% if location %}
Location: {% for word in location.words %}{{ word.text | escapeMarkdown }}{{ ", " if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}{{ (location.geo.latitude + ", " + location.geo.longitude) if location.geo and not location.words.length }}

{% endif %}
{% if bio and not staticFrontPage %}
{% if bio.note %}
{{ bio.note | escapeMarkdown }}

{% endif %}
{% for link in bio.links %}
- [{{ link.label | escapeMarkdown }}]({{ link.url | markdownUrl }})
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
